! mcp_bootstrap_p96.strap -- MCP, printed page 96:
! THE TAIL OF THE TABLE-BUILDING CODE, AND "THE DISPATCHER TOLD MOVE
! TO REJECT NEXT JOB".
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.103, header "PAGE NUMBER 96" --
! read, not assumed: the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID
! 11011IPL  CARD ID 18000698  DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 96",
! and the page's own LOCATION sub-header prints 005365.
!
! Fifty-six lines, forty-four of which compile.  The twelve that do
! not are 6, 16, 18-25, 30 and 31: blank rules and the two boxed
! headings "THE DISPATCHER TOLD MOVE TO REJECT NEXT JOB" (line 20) and
! "A SPECIAL REJECT WHENTHE PPRUN INDEX HAS BEEN STEPPED" (line 24 --
! "WHENTHE" is the page's own spacing).  Card serials run 18000698
! (line 1) to 18000753 (line 56), so the line number is the serial
! minus 18000697; that is how the 56-line count was CONFIRMED rather
! than estimated, and it is what proves no line fell off the top or
! the bottom of the render.
!
! THE LOCATION CHAIN CLOSES END TO END.  005365.40 (line 1) to
! 005424.00 (line 56); every row's printed location plus its half
! words equals the next row's printed location, with no gap and no
! overlap, for all forty-four compiled rows.  Line 56 is a single
! half-word, so the counter reaches 005424.40, which is where printed
! p.97 should begin.  THE JOIN TO p.95 IS NOT CHECKED HERE: p.95 has
! not been read, so this deck asserts only that this page's own header
! says LOCATION 005365 and its line 1 sits at 005365.40.
!
! >>> WHAT THE PAGE DOES. <<<  Lines 1-17 finish laying out the
! tables: LFT loads the unit count T UNCT out of the PP reference word
! and the cumulative multiply at line 2 multiplies it by the unit-area
! table length T UNLGN (printed p.84 line 45 declares it SYN(BU,6),9),
! giving the reel-pool size; T MXF takes the first free cell, the base
! address T LIMB is removed, and T MXC and T MXG are set to the first
! free location.  Line 9 compares the result against T BAMCP, the
! upper bound, and line 10 branches past the error exit.  Lines 11-13
! set error code 4.0 in T MX1 and reject the job; lines 14-15 are the
! zeroing loop T M1F; line 17 goes back to T M1 for the next card.
! Lines 26-29 are T MREJB, the special reject that marks the PP word
! rejected and processed and falls into T MREJS with T MXB activated
! for the count check.  Lines 32-45 are T MREJ proper, the entry the
! dispatcher uses: it picks the next job out of T PPRUN (overlap) or
! T PPURF (not overlap), sets the processed bit, tests and sets the
! reject bit, steps T PPRUN and loads T MXB.  Lines 46-56 are T MREJS
! / T MREJ1, which walk the I/O request table releasing units --
! channel address, multi-channel test, channel number, store into the
! dummy unit area T CAT, unit table address, unit number.
!
! T MREJ at 005402.00 IS THE SYMBOL printed p.88 line 11 branches to
! ("BZRZ,T MREJ", 005402.34 C0).  p.88's deck carried it as a forward
! SYN stand-in at (8)5402.0; this page prints the label itself, in the
! NAME column at line 32, and confirms that address.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT WAS READ, WHAT WAS DERIVED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) EVERY LOCATION AND EVERY BINARY HALF-WORD below was read off the
!     page: the LINE+LOCATION column at 600 dpi, the BINARY OUTPUT
!     column at 900 dpi in four bands, the NAME+STATEMENT column at
!     600 dpi and the five disputed rows again at 1200 dpi.
!
! (2) THE OFF-PAGE SYMBOLS ARE NOT DERIVED FROM THIS PAGE.  Each is
!     carried as a SYN stand-in quoting the page that PRINTS it:
!       p.83  T MX1, T MXA, T MXB, T MXC, T MXF, T MXG, T MXEE
!             (lines 21-29), T LIMB (15), T BAMCP (17), T MAXRF (18)
!       p.80  T PPRUN, T PPURF, T CRREF, T UNCT, T JBPRO, T RJECT
!       p.84  T UNLGN (line 45)
!       p.78  T CHSXW          p.62  T ABSCH, T ABSUN
!       p.63  T MULTI, T UNTBA p.87  T CAT (line 11)
!     Those are the rows that are a REAL check of address placement:
!     the address came from another page's print, and this page's
!     print reproduces it.
!
! (3) FOUR SYMBOLS COULD NOT BE READ ANYWHERE AND ARE DERIVED.  Say so
!     when quoting this deck.  The hazard is that a branch's low octal
!     field is NOT the target's bit offset -- it carries the condition
!     too -- so an address may never be taken off a branch row without
!     a same-operation calibration.  The listing's own format (see
!     strap/listing_oracle.py) is that bit 18, the half-word select,
!     is the TOP bit of the printed octal pair, and the five low bits
!     are the operation.  On this page the calibration is complete for
!     one of the four and partial for three:
!
!       T M1    005021.40   READ-EQUIVALENT.  Line 17 prints
!                           "005021.50 00" for "B,T M1".  Three bare
!                           B rows on THIS page have targets this page
!                           prints outright -- line 13 B,T MREJB
!                           005377.10 against 005377.00, line 35
!                           B,T MREJ7 005405.10 against 005405.00,
!                           line 29 B,T MREJS 005414.10 against
!                           005414.00 -- so a bare B adds 0o10 and
!                           nothing else.  005021.50 - 0o10 =
!                           005021.40, and printed p.88 line 15 prints
!                           "T M1" in its NAME column at 005021.40.
!                           Two independent routes, same value.
!       T N2    005444.00   Line 46 prints "005444.30 42" for
!                           "BXCZ,T N2".  p.88's BZXCZ rows print
!                           0o30 against targets at .00 (line 26,
!                           005026.30 40 for T MLOK1 at 005026.00).
!                           Same low five bits, so the half-word bit
!                           is clear and the target is word-aligned.
!                           DERIVED.
!       T MREJ5 005437.40   Line 50's SECOND half-word prints
!                           "005437.74 00".  0o74 = 111100: top bit
!                           set -> .40.  The 0o34 low part matches the
!                           BB rows (lines 33 and 42) and the BZB1 row
!                           (line 40), all three of which have targets
!                           this page prints -- but BZB is not BB, so
!                           this is a FAMILY calibration, not a
!                           same-operation one.  DERIVED.
!       T MREJ3 005442.00   Line 48 prints "005442.34 C2" for
!                           "BRZ,T MREJ3".  Same reading of the top
!                           bit: 0o34 = 011100, half-word bit clear,
!                           so word-aligned.  NO same-operation
!                           witness anywhere in the corpus.  DERIVED,
!                           and the weakest of the four.
!
!     THE THREE ROWS THAT NAME THEM -- lines 46, 48 and 50 -- THEREFORE
!     CHECK ONLY THEIR OPERATION BITS, because their addresses were
!     taken from these very rows.  Forty-one of the forty-four rows
!     are independent checks; three are not.  Line 50 is half an
!     exception worth keeping: it is two half-words and only the
!     SECOND carries T MREJ5.  Its first, "000000.33 88", encodes
!     T MULTI, which printed p.63 line 2 gives as SYN(BU,1),0.27 and
!     0o33 is 27.  That half IS an independent check.
!
! (4) THE TWO BB ROWS CROSS-CHECK EACH OTHER, which is the cheapest
!     test of the page's most unusual operand.  Line 33 is
!     "BB,0.25($15),T MREJ8" -> 005404.74, with T MREJ8 printed on
!     this page at 005404.40: delta 0o34.  Line 42 is
!     "BB,.25($15),T MREJS-.32" -> 005413.74, and T MREJS is printed
!     at 005414.00, so the operand T MREJS-.32 is 005413.40: delta
!     0o34 again.  Same mnemonic, same trailing byte, same delta, two
!     targets this page prints.  The "-.32" is read correctly.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE 0/C PAIR IS NOT DECIDABLE BY SHAPE ON THIS PAGE EITHER, and
! printed p.88's deck already said why: the SAME field prints open in
! one row and closed in another off the same worn drum. <<<  Three
! places on this page had to be settled by something other than the
! shape:
!
!   line 12  The statement prints "CMOCOO(BU,18),T MAXRF" and the
!            second half-word's trailing byte prints "FC".  printed
!            p.88 line 8 is the same statement against another symbol,
!            "CM0000(BU,18),T ERFLG", and prints "022000.00 F0".  An
!            independently transcribed witness, so: CM0000, and F0.
!   line 33  "BB,C.25($15),T MREJ8".  Line 42 is the same mnemonic
!            with ".25($15)" and NO leading character, and the two
!            rows print the IDENTICAL first half-word, 000000.31 8F.
!            A character that changes no bit between the two rows is a
!            zero.  Written 0.25.
!   line 48  "005442.34 C2" -- the trailing byte.  THIS ONE IS NOT
!            SETTLED BY THE INK AND IS NOT SETTLED BY A WITNESS.
!            p.88 prints C2 for BAE and for BXVLZ, which are different
!            operations; BRZ has no transcribed twin anywhere in the
!            corpus.  The value below is what strap_asm assembles.
!            That is NOT circular -- strap/opcodes.py took BRZ's bits
!            from bsv/StretchDecode.bsv, i.e. from the Reference Card,
!            with no input from this page -- but it is also not a
!            second reading of the INK, and a row settled by the
!            assembler is a row this listing has not checked.
!            RECORDED AS AN UNRESOLVED GLYPH.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ONE SUBSTITUTION
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE LISTING SPELLS CUMULATIVE MULTIPLY IMMEDIATE "*I+" AND THIS
! DECK SPELLS IT "*+I". <<<  Line 2 prints "*I+,T UNLGN,46" -- the
! asterisk is unmistakable at 1200 dpi and is a six-pointed glyph
! plainly unlike the "+" two characters along.  strap_asm implements
! the immediate suffix as C22-6531 Appendix A footnote 4 words it ("may
! be suffixed by the letter I"), i.e. TRAILING, and rejects the infix
! form with "unknown mnemonic '*I+'".  Written "*+I", the row
! assembles to 110000.00 80  406027.23 90 -- the printed word, bit for
! bit, both half-words.  So this is a spelling difference and not a
! different instruction, and it is ALSO the check on T UNLGN: the left
! half-word carries 9 left-justified in a 6-bit field, which is printed
! p.84 line 45's "T UNLGN SYN(BU,6),9" arriving from the other end.
! THE ASSEMBLER LIMITATION IS REAL and is the one this page hit: STRAP
! as IBM shipped it accepted the I between the operation and its
! modifier, and strap_asm does not.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LISTING MARKS: lines 10, 38 and 53 carry the bare "*" after their
! location that printed pp.3, 37-39, 88 and 98 also carry.  It changes
! no compiled bit.

! ---- index names, printed p.83 lines 21-29 ------------------------
TMX1    SYN, $1                      ! p.83 line 21
TMXA    SYN, $2                      ! p.83 line 22 -PP REF WORD LOCATOR
TMXB    SYN, $3                      ! p.83 line 23 -I/O REQ TABLE PICK
TMXC    SYN, $4                      ! p.83 line 24 -SYMB I/O TABLE INDEX
TMXF    SYN, $7                      ! p.83 line 27 -REEL POOL INDEX
TMXG    SYN, $8                      ! p.83 line 28 -TEMPORARY INDEX
TMXEE   SYN, $9                      ! p.83 line 29 -TEMPORARY INDEX
! ---- bounds and limits, printed p.83 lines 15/17/18 ---------------
TLIMB   SYN, (8)2155.0               ! p.83 line 15 -UPPER BOUNDARY
TBAMCP  SYN, (8)2153.0               ! p.83 line 17
TMAXRF  SYN, (8)2155.40              ! p.83 line 18
! ---- the PP reference word, printed p.80 --------------------------
TPPRUN  SYN, (8)3315.0
TPPURF  SYN, (8)3313.0
TCRREF  SYN(BU,18), 0.0
TUNCT   SYN(BU,8), 0.28
TJBPRO  SYN(BU,1), 0.36
TRJECT  SYN(BU,1), 0.37
! ---- the unit area table length, printed p.84 line 45 -------------
TUNLGN  SYN(BU,6), 9
! ---- the I/O request table, printed pp.62, 63 and 78 --------------
TCHSXW  SYN, (8)2152.0               ! p.78
TABSCH  SYN(BU,18), 0.46             ! p.62 line 39 -ABSOLUTE CHANNEL
TABSUN  SYN(BU,3), 0.07              ! p.62 line 34 -UNIT NUMBER
TMULTI  SYN(BU,1), 0.27              ! p.63 line 2  -MULTI-CHANNEL BIT
TUNTBA  SYN(BU,18), 0.0              ! p.63 line 1  -UNIT TABLE ADDRESS
! ---- the dummy unit area, printed p.87 line 11 --------------------
TCAT    SYN, (8)4771.0
! ---- backward, onto printed p.88 ----------------------------------
TM1     SYN, (8)5021.40              ! p.88 line 15 prints the label
! ---- DERIVED, see (3) above: NOT read anywhere ---------------------
TN2     SYN, (8)5444.0
TMREJ3  SYN, (8)5442.0
TMREJ5  SYN, (8)5437.40

        SLC, (8)5365.40

        LFT, TUNCT(TMXA)             ! line 1  -THE NO. OF UNITS REQ
                                      !           TO FACTOR REG
        *+I, TUNLGN, 46              ! line 2  -ADD UNIT AREA TBL
                                      !     LENGHT  (card: "*I+")
        LV, TMXF, $R                 ! line 3  -FIRST CELL AVAIL FOR
                                      !           REEL NUMBER
        -(BU,18), TLIMB, 46          ! line 4  -REMOVE THE BASE ADDRESS
        LV, TMXC, TLIMB              ! line 5  -FIRST LOC AVAL FOR SYM
                                      !           I/O LOC TBL

        LV, TMXG, TLIMB              ! line 7  -PREPARE FOR TABLE ZEROING
        LC, TMXG, $R                 ! line 8
        KV, TMXF, TBAMCP             ! line 9  -IS THE REEL POOL
                                      !           EXCEEDING BOUNDS
        BXL, TM1F                    ! line 10 -IF WITHIN PP ALLOWED
                                      !           LIMMITS           (*)
        LVI, TMX1, 4.0               ! line 11 -NOTE THE ERROR-
                                      !           OUTSIDE LIMITS
        CM0000(BU,18), TMAXRF        ! line 12
        B, TMREJB                    ! line 13 -AND REJECT JOB
TM1F    Z, 0.0(TMXG)                 ! line 14 -ZERO THE SLOTS
        CB+, TMXG, TM1F              ! line 15

        B, TM1                       ! line 17 -GET THE FIRST CARD

! ---- A SPECIAL REJECT WHENTHE PPRUN INDEX HAS BEEN STEPPED --------
TMREJB  CM1111, TRJECT(TMXA)         ! line 26
        CM1111, TJBPRO(TMXA)         ! line 27 -SET THE JOB PROCESSED
                                      !           BIT ON
        V+I, TMXB, 0.0               ! line 28 -TO ACTIVATE IX FOR
                                      !           COUNT CHECK
        B, TMREJS                    ! line 29

! ---- THE DISPATCHER TOLD MOVE TO REJECT NEXT JOB -------------------
TMREJ   LVI, TMXEE, 0.0              ! line 32
        BB, 0.25($15), TMREJ8        ! line 33 -IF NOT OVERLAP
        LX, TMXA, TPPRUN             ! line 34 -GET THE NEXT JOB TO
                                      !           BE RUN
        B, TMREJ7                    ! line 35
TMREJ8  LX, TMXA, TPPURF             ! line 36 -SET UP FOR NOT OVERLAP
TMREJ7  L, TCRREF(TMXA), 46          ! line 37 -I/O REQ TABLE ADDRESS
        LF, TUNCT(TMXA), 18          ! line 38 -THE NUMBER OF UNITS
                                      !           TO CF              (*)
        CM1111, TJBPRO(TMXA)         ! line 39 -SET THE JOB PROCESSED BIT
        BZB1, TRJECT(TMXA), TMREJ6   ! line 40 -TEST AND SET THE
                                      !           REJECT BIT
        Z, $R                        ! line 41 -CLEAR ACC IF ALREADY
                                      !           REJECTED
        BB, .25($15), TMREJS-.32     ! line 42 -IF BYPASS
TMREJ6  V+ICR, TMXA, 2.0             ! line 43
        SX, TMXA, TPPRUN             ! line 44 -ADVANCE AND SAVE FOR
                                      !           NEXT JOB
        LX, TMXB, $R                 ! line 45
TMREJS  BXCZ, TN2                    ! line 46 -IF NO REQ TO ZERO
TMREJ1  L, TABSCH(TMXB), 46          ! line 47 -GET ADDRESS OF CHANNEL
        BRZ, TMREJ3                  ! line 48
        LV, TMXG, $R                 ! line 49
        BZB, TMULTI(TMXG), TMREJ5    ! line 50 -IF A NON-MULTI CHANNEL
        -(BU,18), TCHSXW, 46         ! line 51 -COMPUTE THE CHANNEL
                                      !           NUMBER
        ST(BU,7), TCAT+.12, 46       ! line 52
        L, TUNTBA(TMXG), 46          ! line 53 -GET UNIT TABLE ADDRESS
                                      !                              (*)
        LV, TMXG, $R                 ! line 54
        L, TABSUN(TMXB), 46          ! line 55 -GET THE UNIT NUMBER
        V+, TMXG, $R                 ! line 56 -ADD TO INITIAL UNIT
                                      !           ADDRESS

